Sat May 12 16:10:23 2001    <reddy@MAGNOLIA>

	* vrml2defs.c: make the default SFBool value be -1, i.e. not 1 or
 	0. This default value is used to suppress output of fields that
 	have a default value set, however, different VRML nodes have
 	different default SFBool values (e.g. AudioClip.loop = FALSE,
 	Collision.collide = TRUE), thus it was possible to set a non-
 	default value for a node, but not have this value output to the
 	VRML file. If there is a better way to do this, then feel free to
 	do it.

